<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* The two faces first paint needs. This was a <ResourcePreloader /> element that resolves to
       no component in the solution: Blazor emits an unknown element as literal markup, so it
       shipped as dead tags to the browser and nothing was ever preloaded. With font-display:swap
       that put the system sans on every cold load — the platform face the design refuses. *@
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/b612-latin-400-normal.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/b612-mono-latin-400-normal.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["KsaMods.Web.styles.css"]" />
    <ImportMap />

    @*
        Order matters and it is the opposite of what it looks like. Browsers walk these and keep
        the *last* one whose type they support, so the raster fallback goes first and the SVG
        last. Declaring the SVG first is how you end up shipping a vector favicon that no browser
        ever uses.

        Both are the same orbit mark, so the fallback is not a different logo either way.
    *@
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="128x128" href="favicon.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="favicon.svg" />

    @*
        Deliberately inline and deliberately blocking, before any stylesheet has painted.

        A stored theme has to reach the root element in the same frame the document does. Do it
        in a module and it lands after first paint, which is the white flash every dark-mode
        visitor sees on a site that got this wrong. It is a few lines, so the cost of blocking
        here is far smaller than the cost of not.
    *@
    <script>
        (function () {
            try {
                var choice = localStorage.getItem('ksamods.theme');
                if (choice === 'dark' || choice === 'light') {
                    document.documentElement.classList.add(choice);
                }
            } catch (e) {
                /* Storage blocked; fall through to the system preference. */
            }
        })();
    </script>

    <HeadOutlet />
</head>

<body>
    @*
        The direction contract, emitted rather than authored as markup: Razor strips HTML comments
        from .razor files, so a plain <!-- --> here would never reach the browser and a contract
        the build erases is one nobody can audit against the render.
    *@
    @DirectionContract

    <Routes />
    <ReconnectModal />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// First child of the body, so it tops the served document and survives the production build.
    /// Checked by grepping the built output for THESIS.
    /// </summary>
    private static readonly MarkupString DirectionContract = new("""
        <!--
        THESIS: The catalogue as the drawing that says which parts mate, and marks where two fight
        for the same pin. Refuses the dark package-registry grid - icon cards, counts, an install
        button - which is what this site shipped as and what every mod index already is.
        OWN-WORLD: A sheet, not an application chrome. Graphite ground or vellum print, hairline
        rules doing the separating instead of elevation, square corners, B612 throughout - the
        face Airbus drew for cockpit displays. Reference blue carries links and actions; drafting
        red is spent only where something is wrong with a mod.
        STORY: A visitor arrives holding a build number, reads the title block for what was
        verified and when, and sees a collision drawn as two callouts claiming one pin.
        FIRST VIEWPORT: Listing - the sheet framed, name and id at the head, the title block
        holding id, revision, bound and verified-at; releases ruled beneath.
        FORM: Interface control document, 3rd on my ordered list, seed b12cf9d3.
        FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review,
        the verdict, and DESIGN.md
        -->
        """);
}
